+    
+    This checks whether the handle was opened for overlapped (asynchronous) I/O.
+    On Windows, handles opened with FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED support overlapped I/O.
+    
+    Note: We cannot test this by actually associating with an IOCP because once
+    a handle is associated with an IOCP, it cannot be associated with another.
+    Instead, we assume that valid handles passed to this module are properly
+    opened for overlapped use (as they come from the collector's pipe factory).
+    For handles that don't support overlapped I/O, the actual I/O operations
+    will fail appropriately.
     """
